  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Alpha. Breaking: tmux_run no longer answers as an MCP task. It blocks until the command exits, for every client, because an SDK task carried no durable tmux handle and a client that disconnected lost work it believed was parked; use tmux_start_job and tmux_job for work that outlives a call. Added: an experimental query-only psmux preview for native Windows and WSL interop, a separate analyzer-clean API that reads one isolated session, its windows and panes, and pane text. Its accepted client is the psmux.exe published in the psmux v3.3.8 release, pinned by SHA-256 and checked before every launch; the caller supplies the executable and LibTmux never bundles or downloads one. Also added TmuxEventsDroppedEvent, which reports per-report and cumulative counts instead of silently dropping control-stream notifications. Hardened: MCP tail cursors are authenticated, bounded, and tied to one endpoint, server generation and pane; every serialized tool result obeys hard line and UTF-8 byte ceilings; Tasks admit at most eight active executions; background jobs retain their originating endpoint and generation instead of cross-routing. The public API is not settled and may change without notice between prereleases; pin an exact version. Full history: https://github.com/libtmux/libtmux-dotnet/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
